In short (this summary is not the license; the full text governs):

- You may copy and give away the unmodified source freely, keeping the
  copyright notices and disclaimers.
- You may modify it if every changed file carries a prominent notice of
  how and when it was changed, and the changes are made freely
  available (or one of the other options in clause 3 is met).
- Binaries you distribute must come with the source or with
  instructions for getting it, or give modified programs names that do
  not clash with the standard ones (clause 4).
- You may charge a reasonable copying fee, but not a fee for the
  package itself (clause 5).
- The author's name may not be used to promote derived works without
  permission (clause 9).
- There is no warranty (clause 10).

This fork (https://github.com/dleecurt/craft) meets clause 3 with a
change notice at the top of every modified file, by publishing all
changes in a public repository, and by listing the differences from the
Standard Version in README.md. See LICENSE-NOTES.md for the history of
the license statements.
